# Gate-changing paths. GitHub requests a review from the owner.
#
# The main ruleset does not require that review. The owner is the only maintainer, and GitHub will not let the
# pull request author approve their own pull request, so a required code-owner review would deadlock every change
# on these paths, including Renovate's metadata updates. The request is the signal to read the diff before merging:
# a pull request can turn a required job into a skip, and a skip satisfies the ruleset (ADR-0012, amended 2026-11-06).

/.github/                          @PCritchfield
/.gitleaks.toml                    @PCritchfield
/renovate.json                     @PCritchfield
/gradle/verification-metadata.xml  @PCritchfield
/gradle/osv-scanner.toml           @PCritchfield
